<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyaxares</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cyaxares the Mede, Cyaxares of Media</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cyaxares was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> in the late seventh and early sixth centuries BCE and the main architect of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a>. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabopolassar">Nabopolassar</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, he sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> in 614 BCE and helped destroy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> in 612 BCE. The alliance brought down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and opened the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyaxares.jpg" alt="Cyaxares" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:18._Detail._The_facade_of_the_rock-cut_tombs_of_Qizqapan,_Sulaymaniyah_Governorate,_Iraqi_Kurdistan._Probably_Achaemenid_(6th-5th_century_BCE)_rather_than_Median.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
